    "updated_at": "2026-11-20T07:49:53Z",
    "body": "This is  starting point issue. Most lathes defines their WCS at a center of the part. This doesnt mean that the cutter starts from center, it just means that it references it. The fault would be that the cutter moves to the starting point as a first move. It doesnt have to.. This is a general Post processing problem. The machine should move to its first starting point for an operation.. In relation to the WCS.. not start at the WCS.. It doesnt matter where the WCS is. The first operation starts where it has to start to clear the part, but in relation to the WCS.",
